# mem_copy_index_join.tkr — the RM-C2 index-join fixture (crumb 0020). `main.tks` zero-fills a
# 5-byte `dst`, copies a 3-byte `src` into `dst[1..4]` via `teko::runtime::copy`, and exits 0 only
# if every byte lands at its exact index (the untouched positions still zero, the copied run
# byte-exact) and `dst.len` stays 5 (no growth). `src/` does not yet call `copy`, so this path is
# not fixpoint-exercised.

Feature: mem_copy_index_join — copy(dst, at, src) writes dst[at + i] = src[i] with no growth

  Scenario: copy_writes_the_exact_index_range_and_leaves_the_rest_zero
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
